<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's Bozano sees Banerj auction in Nov.</title>
<headline>Brazil's Bozano sees Banerj auction in Nov.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rio de Janeiro state bank Banerj will likely be privatized in late November, once its healthy portion is broken off and sold as a new bank.</p>
<p>Under the plan, brokerage arm Banerj Distribuidora de Titulos e Valores Mobiliarios will receive a capital injection and transformed into a bank, said Paulo Ferraz, the head of the firm assigned to manage Banerj and prepare it for privatization.</p>
<p>&quot;We will increase the brokerage's capital and transform into a bank. This new bank will be sold,&quot; said Ferraz, president of private bank Bozano, Simonsen.</p>
</text>
